{"content":[{"c":["HAZAZON-TAMAR"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["City identifiable with En-gedi in ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.20.2","r":"2Chr.20.2","rawR":"2Chr.20.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.20.2","value":"2Chr.20.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chronicles 20:2"},". During the time of Abraham, it was inhabited by Amorites who were subdued by Kedorlaomer as he and other eastern kings swept through the area (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.14.7","r":"Gen.14.7","rawR":"Gen.14.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.14.7","value":"Gen.14.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 14:7"},"). It has been suggested that it may be the Tamar that Solomon fortified (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.9.18","r":"1Kgs.9.18","rawR":"1Kgs.9.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.9.18","value":"1Kgs.9.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 9:18"},"), placed by Ezekiel southeast of Israel (",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.47.18-19","r":"Ezek.47.18-19","rawR":"Ezek.47.18-19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.47.18-19","value":"Ezek.47.18-19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 47:18-19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.48.28","r":"Ezek.48.28","rawR":"Ezek.48.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.48.28","value":"Ezek.48.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"48:28"},"). Wadi Hasasa has apparently been named after the ancient site."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"HazazonTamar","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Chronicles 20:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.20.2","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.20.2","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.20.2"},{"anchorText":"Gn 14:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.14.7","rawQueryValue":"Gen.14.7","sourceRefExact":"Gen.14.7"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 9:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.9.18","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.9.18","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.9.18"},{"anchorText":"Ez 47:18-19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.47.18-19","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.47.18-19","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.47.18-19"},{"anchorText":"48:28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.48.28","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.48.28","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.48.28"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"c6f2cc3de78016d74909e81149dea7405a361a59647857efbed27d94f5b258d4","sourceItemName":"HazazonTamar","sourceItemOrder":179,"sourceMember":"Articles/H.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"HazazonTamar","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Hazazon-Tamar","title":"Hazazon-Tamar","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}